target:    composer.json
gate:      composer test:composer-script-closure
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    is reachable from neither test:all nor the standalone list
rationale: Drops test:no-orphan-test-files from the test:all closure while leaving its definition. The script then runs only if someone types it -- the state test:fp-negative-linux was found in, reachable from nothing and running nowhere, which the file-level orphan gate cannot see because it only asks whether a FILE is named.
---
--- a/composer.json
+++ b/composer.json
@@ -366,7 +366,6 @@
       "@test:version-suffix-contract",
       "@test:databuckets-week-start",
       "@test:consent-plugins-active-step",
-      "@test:no-orphan-test-files",
       "@test:composer-script-closure",
       "@test:browscap-fileinfo-preflight",
       "@test:consent-filter-context"
